## BENCHMARK TARGETS (PERFORMANCE GUARDS)

### Target 1: CartesianProductJoin (fillRepeated)

**Baseline**: Scalar copy (1 element per cycle)
**Target**: AVX2 vectorized fill (4 elements per cycle)
**Expected Improvement**: 100-150% (2x-2.5x speedup)
**Threshold**: 80% improvement (1.8x speedup minimum)

**Validation**: `BM_CartesianProduct_AVX2` vs `BM_CartesianProduct_Scalar`
**Guard**: `if (speedup < 1.8) { FAIL }`

### Target 2: IndexScan (decompressVarInt)

**Baseline**: Scalar VarInt decode (byte-by-byte)
**Target**: AVX2 continuation bit detection (32 bytes parallel)
**Expected Improvement**: 50-100% (1.5x-2x speedup)
**Threshold**: 40% improvement (1.4x speedup minimum)

**Validation**: `BM_IndexScan_Decompress_AVX2` vs `BM_IndexScan_Decompress_Scalar`
**Guard**: `if (speedup < 1.4) { FAIL }`

### Target 3: GroupBy (aggregateColumn)

**Baseline**: Scalar SUM/MIN/MAX (1 element per cycle)
**Target**: AVX2 parallel aggregation (4 elements per cycle)
**Expected Improvement**: 80-120% (1.8x-2.2x speedup)
**Threshold**: 64% improvement (1.64x speedup minimum)

**Validation**: `BM_GroupBy_SUM_AVX2` vs `BM_GroupBy_SUM_Scalar`
**Guard**: `if (speedup < 1.64) { FAIL }`

### Target 4: Filter (evaluate)

**Baseline**: Scalar comparison (1 row per cycle)
**Target**: AVX2 batch comparison (4 rows per cycle)
**Expected Improvement**: 120-200% (2.2x-3x speedup)
**Threshold**: 96% improvement (1.96x speedup minimum)

**Validation**: `BM_Filter_Comparison_AVX2` vs `BM_Filter_Comparison_Scalar`
**Guard**: `if (speedup < 1.96) { FAIL }`

### Overall Target (TPC-H Benchmark)

**Baseline**: TPC-H queries with SIMD disabled
**Target**: 30-50% overall improvement (join/filter/aggregation heavy queries)
**Threshold**: 24% improvement (80% of 30% target)

**Validation**: TPC-H Q1, Q3, Q6, Q9, Q17 runtime comparison
**Guard**: `if (overall_improvement < 0.24) { FAIL }`

---

## REGRESSION GUARDS

### Regression 1: SIMD Disabled Performance

**Guard**: Performance with SIMD disabled must be identical to pre-SIMD baseline (±2%)

**Validation**: Run TPC-H with `enableSIMD*=false`, compare to baseline
**Threshold**: -2% to +2% variance (no regression, no improvement)
**Verdict**: `if (|variance| > 0.02) { FAIL }`

### Regression 2: Backward Compatibility

**Guard**: Old indexes (v7-v15) must load successfully with SIMD enabled

**Validation**: Load each version, run query `SELECT ?s ?p ?o LIMIT 1000`
**Threshold**: 100% success rate (9/9 versions load)
**Verdict**: `if (failures > 0) { FAIL }`

### Regression 3: Correctness Equivalence

**Guard**: SIMD results must be bit-identical to scalar results (all 55+ tests)

**Validation**: `test/engine/simd/SimdCorrectnessTest.cpp`
**Threshold**: 100% test pass rate (55/55 tests green)
**Verdict**: `if (test_failures > 0) { FAIL }`

