## ROLLBACK PROCEDURES (DETERMINISTIC)

### Rollback Trigger Matrix

| Trigger Condition | Detection Method | Rollback Action | Timeline Impact |
|-------------------|------------------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Correctness failure (SIMD != Scalar) | `SimdCorrectnessTest` failure | Set `enableSIMD*=false` | +1 week (P4: 4 weeks) |
| Performance regression (SIMD slower) | `validate-simd-performance.sh` failure | Tune thresholds or disable | +0-1 week |
| TPC-H query failure | Phase 4 integration test failure | Disable failing component | +1 week |
| Deserialization error (VERSION_SIMD) | Phase 4 backward compat test failure | Revert to VERSION_1 only | +1 week |
| Memory overhead >10% | Phase 4 memory profiling | Disable IdTableAOS, use SOA | +0 week (acceptable) |

### Rollback Procedure (Week 11-12)

**Step 1** (Day 1): Immediate mitigation
```bash
# Disable all SIMD flags via runtime parameters
export QLEVER_ENABLE_SIMD_FILTER=false
export QLEVER_ENABLE_SIMD_GROUPBY=false
export QLEVER_ENABLE_SIMD_JOIN=false
export QLEVER_ENABLE_SIMD_SERIALIZATION=false

# Re-run failing test
./test/engine/simd/SimdCorrectnessTest  # Must pass with SIMD disabled
```

**Step 2** (Week 11): Code rollback
```bash
# Revert SIMD commits (Week 6-9)
git revert [P3E-W6-1]..[P3E-W9-2]

# Verify codebase returns to pre-SIMD state
git diff baseline..HEAD  # Should be empty (ignoring other Phase 3 work)
```

**Step 3** (Week 12): Validation
```bash
# Re-run Phase 4 integration tests
./scripts/run-tpch-benchmark.sh --simd-disabled

# Verify no regression vs. pre-SIMD baseline
python3 scripts/compare-benchmark-results.py baseline.json current.json
# Expected: ±2% variance (no performance change)
```

**Rollback Cost**: +1-2 weeks (Phase 4 extended from 3 weeks to 4-5 weeks)

